T_{\\rm GW}=\\frac{12}{19}\\frac{c_{0}^{4}}{\\beta}\\int_{0}^{e}de\\frac{x^{29/19}[ 1+(121/304)x^{2}]^{1181/2299}}{(1-x^{2})^{3/2}}\\,, Figure 3: The LISA detection range of systems considered in Fig. 2, with detection threshold SNR set to be 15. The orbit is assumed to be circular for simplicity. with

c_{0}=a(1-e^{2})e^{-12/19}\\left[1+\\frac{121}{304}e^{2}\\right]^{-870/2 299},\\quad\\beta=\\frac{64}{5}\\frac{G^{3}M_{1}M_{2}(M_{1}+M_{2})}{c^{5}}  as shown in the right panel of Fig. 2. These timescales are order of thousands of years for stellar-mass binaries, which are much shorter than the typical lifetimes of field binaries 3. As T_{\\rm GW}\\propto a^{4} and T_{\\rm prec}\\propto a^{5/2}, it is reasonable to expect that the distribution of similar systems in precession time should be

